A||N||4||Seanh||Broken Ball Joint, NEW!||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||10-17-2001||03:54 PM||||Last night my passenger side, lower front ball joint just broke. Shortly after a nice race at about 120 mph (would have sucked to have broken then..) It happened to wait till I pulled in the gas station and was backing up, then snapped the stud off the ball, below the treads and the control arm drug on the ground, wheel is wedged between the fender and ground and very akward position...<P>Anyway, I bought these ball joints new, the summer, from the Fiero Store...I had them pressed in and  installed everything else myself. So has anyone else had any problems with the Fiero Store ball joints not holding up, or was this just a freak deal? I don't want to drive around with the other one on there is there is really any doubt of their quality...<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 4spd Auto, getting ready to install T-6 turbo.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||10-17-2001||04:02 PM||||Yeesh!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||jelly2m8||10-17-2001||04:47 PM||||It's possible that the ball joint was defective. <BR> <BR> It is also possible that the nut was improperly torqued down. If the nut was too loose, it could have broken there, but check the hole in the spindle, and make sure that it is still round, and not oblong. Also the stud of the ball joint show show signs of bending if it was loose.<P> It's possible that the nut was too tight, but usually you will strip the treads out of the nut long before you damage the ball joint.<P>   Who knows? Anything is possible.<P> Check with the Fierostore, they may warranty it.<P> Be thankful that it didn't break at 120 mph!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||10-17-2001||11:01 PM||||I got a couple from them, can't remember if it was uppers or lowers, recently.  I would be interested, because I will keep a much closer eye on things.  Do check your parts to make sure the spindle isn't messed up before replacing the ball joint.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>Edited for my laziness and stupidity...didn't read thoroughly enough.<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 10-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||10-17-2001||11:05 PM||||Its an 86. I do have WS6 springs on a non-stock WS6 car, but I doubt that could make a difference like this. I didn't check the spindle for anything other then looking out of round to the eye, I just replaced the ball joints. Anyway, since I'm in school all day I'm having it done by a garage so it should be all ready tomarrow and I can look more closely at the broken ball joint. ||||reg||1
